    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nModel versioning, API latency, monitoring, data drift, security, scalability, and integration with existing systems.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks breadth, but the useful signal is whether you can explain what the important items are for and distinguish the ones that are commonly confused.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Model versioning, API latency, monitoring, data drift, security, scalability, and integration with existing systems.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nName the common items first and give a short purpose for each. Spend most of the time on the distinction most likely to matter in the role.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. Model versioning, API latency, monitoring, data drift, security, scalability, and integration with existing systems.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn an ML workflow, what are the challenges in deploying ml models matters when data quality, model behavior, evaluation, or production cost is affected. The method should be validated on representative data rather than inferred from training results alone.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Reciting names without explaining their purpose.\n- Missing the common options while focusing on obscure variants.\n- Giving an exhaustive list when the question only asks for the important examples.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nGive the common answers first and attach one useful distinction or use case to each instead of reciting a long list.",
