    shortDescription: "Explain shard key selection.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nShard key determines data distribution across shards. It should have high cardinality, low frequency, and be used in most queries to enable targeted operations. Choose a key that evenly distributes writes and reads.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks breadth, but the useful signal is whether you can explain what the important items are for and distinguish the ones that are commonly confused.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Shard key determines data distribution across shards.\n2. It should have high cardinality, low frequency, and be used in most queries to enable targeted operations.\n3. Choose a key that evenly distributes writes and reads.\n4. Tie the explanation to data shape, access pattern, concurrency, and the evidence you would use to judge performance or correctness..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nName the common items first and give a short purpose for each. Spend most of the time on the distinction most likely to matter in the role.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. Shard key determines data distribution across shards.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a data-backed service, what are the considerations for choosing shard key matters when correctness, access patterns, concurrency, and query or storage cost have to work together. Measure the real workload rather than assuming a design choice is always beneficial.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Reciting names without explaining their purpose.\n- Missing the common options while focusing on obscure variants.\n- Giving an exhaustive list when the question only asks for the important examples.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nGive the common answers first and attach one useful distinction or use case to each instead of reciting a long list.",
