    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nA shard key is a field or set of fields used to distribute documents across shards. It determines the range of values that belong to each shard. Choosing a good shard key is critical for even distribution and query performance.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain a shard key accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. A shard key is a field or set of fields used to distribute documents across shards.\n2. It determines the range of values that belong to each shard.\n3. Choosing a good shard key is critical for even distribution and query performance.\n4. Tie the explanation to data shape, access pattern, concurrency, and the evidence you would use to judge performance or correctness..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nLead with the distinction that matters most. Then connect it to behavior, a practical consequence, and one limitation.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. A shard key is a field or set of fields used to distribute documents across shards.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. A shard key is a field or set of fields used to distribute documents across shards.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Assuming a schema or index is automatically faster without checking access patterns.\n- Ignoring concurrency or consistency requirements.\n- Quoting performance characteristics without measured evidence.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nStay close to the exact question. One technically precise example is more valuable than a broad overview of the entire technology.",
